+FILE/METADATA
 FILENAME           19841015-ia209_iGFZ_kPORT2025d_v000_bIonoFree.snx
 TITLE              GFZ VLBI normal equation for  EOP, TRF, and CRF
 ALTERNATIVE        GFZ VLBI normal equation
 ABSTRACT            SINEX file of GFZ VLBI normal equation for IVS EOP
                    station, and source coordinates (single technique
                    combination).  Standards, models and parameterization are
                    choosen with respect to the IERS and IVS conventions.
 IDENTIFIER         gfz2025d
 STATUS             completed
 LANGUAGE           en
 CHARSET            utf-8
 DATE               2026-04-25 19:32:60
 DATETYPE           creation
 FORMATNAME         SINEX
 FORMATVERSION      2.02
 MEDIUMNAME         onLine
 LINKAGE            
 SUPPLEMENTALINFO   This file contains the normal equation matrix of the GFZ
                    least-squares solution of a VLBI-session from the IVS data
                    center. Only DB version 4 or higher are analyzed. The
                    provided solution is always based on the available highest
                    version of the input database.
                    Parameters:
                    a. source positions
                    b. station positions
                    c. Earth orientation: pole coordinates, UT1-UTC, dX, and dY
                       as piece-wise-linear continuous functions
                    d. Zenith troposphere (per station): parameterized to be
                       values of a piece-wise-linear continuous function with a
                       temporal resolution of 30 min, relative constrained
                       with 11 mm/sqrt(30 min) parameters are reduced (only
                       implicitly included).
                    e. Troposphere gradient: parameterized to be values of
                       a piece-wise-linear continuous function with a temporal
                       resolution of 4 hours, relative constrained with
                       2 mm/sqrt(4h),
                       parameters are reduced (only implicitly included).
                    f. Clock model (per station w.r.t. reference station):
                       coefficients of a parabola, for each modeled clock break
                       one more parabola; as well as a piece-wise-linear
                       continuous function with a temporal resolution of
                       30 min, relative constrained with 10 mm/sqrt(30 min)
                       parameters are reduced (only implicitly included).
                    g. This SINEX file contains the two (non-standard) blocks 
                       SOLUTION/NORMAL_CALIBRATION LOADING_EFFECT and 
                       SOLUTION/CALIBRATION_ESTIMATE LOADING_EFFECT to allow the
                       retroactive removal of non-tidal atmospheric loading
                       corrections. Note that the apriori values listed in block
                       SOLUTION/APRIORI do include the non-tidal atmospheric
                       loading corrections. For details see: 
                         https://ivscc.gsfc.nasa.gov/IVS_AC/ITRF2020/
                         Pressure_loading_in_sinex_v2020Jan14.pdf
 TOPICCATEGORY      geoscientificInformation
