*
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*
+FILE/COMMENT
 Analysis description - template by Axel Nothnagel
 Version 2.0 (2011-05-26)
 (https://www.ccivs.bkg.bund.de/index.php?uri=bid)
 (see also ftp://ivscc.gsfc.nasa.gov/pub/forms/opac-form.txt)
 1. Origin of input data
     d) other use vgosDB file content version 022
 2. Authentic processing steps after data retrieval
     c) other (Ambiguity resolution taken from vgosDB dataset.
        All other model calculations and analysis steps are performed
        using the PORT analysis software package.)
 3. Origin of meteorological data
     pressure:  c) other use vgosDB file content
     temperature:  c) other use vgosDB file content
 4. Use numerical weather model
     a) none
 5. Setting of mapping functions
     b) other (created by PORT)
 6. Origin of cable cal data
     c) other use vgosDB file content
 7. Application of cable cal flags
     a) all on by default (data from input dataset are used as is)
 8. Selection/settings of geophysical models
 8.1 A priori Earth orientation
     - A priori precession/nutation model: IAU_2006/2000A
     - A priori EOP: eopc04_20u23.1962-now
       using standard nutation offsets dX and dY
     - A priori short-period tidal variations in polar motion and UT1:
     - ocean tides: desai_model_jgrb51665
       libration in polar motion ON
       libration in UT1 ON
     - EOP interpolation: linear
 8.2 A priori geophysical models
     - Solid Earth tides: IERS2010
     - Tidal ocean loading: FES2004
     - Tidal atmosphere loading: gsfc
     - Non-tidal atmosphere loading: GFZ_NTAL
     - Non-tidal oceanic loading: None
     - Non-tidal sea-level loading: None
     - Pole tide: linear IERS20180201
     - Hydrology loading: None
     - Antenna thermal deformation: IVS antenna thermal expansion model of
       Nothnagel (2008) using scan-wise temperatures from vgosDB data
     - Axis offsets: taken from Axel Nothnagel's file
       antenna-info.txt
 8.3 Others
     - A priori TRF: ITRF2020-u2024
     - A priori CRF: icrf3
     - A priori troposphere gradients: apg
     - Mapping functions: VM1
 9. Parameterization
 Information about constraints refer only to the SOLUTION/ESTIMATE block and
 pre-reduced parameters. The SOLUTION/NORMAL_EQUATION_MATRIX block is without
 constraints.
 9.1 Clocks
     b) other (piece-wise linear offsets + one rate
        + one squared rate per station
        with 30 min interval and constraints 1.0 cm after 30 min
 9.2 Atmospheres
     b) other: piece-wise linear function:
        zenith wet delay: 30 min offsets with rel. constr. 1.1 cm after 30 min
        troposphere horizontal gradients:
        240 min offsets, rel. constr. 0.2 cm / 240 min
 10. Outlier elimination
     c) observations with QualityCode from input dataset lower than
        1 0
        for the frequency-ordered bands were flagged
        + residuals larger than 5.0*aposteriori variance of unit weight
        + obvious outliers manually removed
 11. Handling of source positions
     c) Estimate all sources, applying NNR relative to ICRF3
 12. Generation of pre-reduced datum-free normal equations
     b) Program is based on authentic classical least squares adjustment and
        matrix elements of interest are squeezed out by inversion steps.
        vT*P*v = lT*P*l_red - xT*b
        lT*P*l_red = lT*P*l - b2T*inv(N22)*b2
 13.
     - Cut-off elevation angle:  0.0 degree
